KILLTABLE1B -- #568 (vmedefaultkill) kill table 1b, measured 2026-10-20 by the measuring seat (Opus 5.5).  It closes
the two gaps KILLTABLE1_VS_PRETABLE.out named in OBSERVATIONS (c): no leg built "a cased WRITE path broken" (t1cmp rt
and cased wr saw no leg) and none built "a label added AT 0x90" (p1 p2 edge).
Fix: scratchpad vme/fix/dev_vme.fix568.c md5 4e3e7fc220062b429f7d9d6e140fec9e.  Detector: the SAME frozen copy table 1
used, killtable1/vme_default_probe.frozen.py (md5 19de15b3ea69af28e437cdf92e22c97e), and that copy alone.
Clone: WSL /tmp/gxkt568b from `git archive 1a59a47e' (1a59a47e3ebbb648f06268ab790f901cbc71c88a), configure + make -j4;
each leg = ONE exact find/replace on fix568 (mk_legs568b.py; legs/<LEG>.diff); dev_vme.o + machine_mvme88k.o + gxemul
removed before every build and `[ gxemul -nt <source> ]' checked after it (RUNLOG.txt, build/<LEG>.build.log); driver
kt568b.sh = table 1's kt568.sh with only its locations changed.  This script refuses any raw lacking
VME_DEFAULT_PROBE_DONE.  Predictions = PRETABLE1B.txt (the coordinator's, verbatim), written BEFORE the first build;
MATCH = every predicted row red, no red row outside the predicted rows plus the prediction's own allowance, CONTROL
as predicted where named, and a named numerator (987/988) equal to the measured one.  The seat's reading (also in
PRETABLE1B.txt) is compared in the last field.

