== OBSERVATIONS ==
(a) The gaps: table 1 left 10 rows with no killing leg (neg apparatus, session, live, vbr reset, t1cmp rt, free ctl, free quiet, free neg ctl, cased wr, unasm); after table 1b, 7: neg apparatus, session, live, vbr reset, free quiet, free neg ctl, unasm.
    Closed by 1b: t1cmp rt (by M_T1CMPWRDROP); free ctl (by M_T1CMPWRDROP); cased wr (by M_DROPIRQEN).
    p1 p2 edge already had kills in table 1 (M_EXIT, M_DROPMISC, M_FLTBREAK), but not from its named mutant "a label
    added AT 0x90"; M_ADD90 now reds it (measured: 0x0/0x10010/0x0/0x0 r5=0x1234 r6=0x0).
    Rows still red under no leg of either table: neg apparatus, session, live, vbr reset, free quiet, free neg ctl, unasm.  Of those, CONTROL rows: neg apparatus, session, live, vbr reset, free quiet, free neg ctl, unasm; the null medium (table 1's NULL.raw)
    reds vbr reset, free neg ctl.  These are apparatus controls whose job is to stay green; PRETABLE section 4 lists unasm / live / neg
    apparatus / vbr reset / free ctl / free quiet as apparatus, and the addendum added session and free neg ctl as
    controls -- none of them is a channel aimed at a dev_vme.c mutant.
(b) M_DROPIRQEN     CONTROL=FAIL; red CONTROL rows: cased census; red non-control rows: cased wr.
(b) M_T1CMPWRDROP   CONTROL=FAIL; red CONTROL rows: t1cmp rt, free ctl; red non-control rows: NONE.
(b) M_ADD90         CONTROL=OK; red CONTROL rows: none; red non-control rows: p1 fault lo, p1 fault wr, p1 p2 edge, p1 census.
    A leg seen only through CONTROL rows reds a gate (the probe exits 1) under the CONTROL reason, not under a row
    of its own -- the shape table 1's M_DROPTCTL showed for cased census (KILLTABLE1_VS_PRETABLE.out, MISS NOTES).
